                <pb facs="0406" n="392" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg392"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/11–944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-11T16:00:00-04:00">November 11, 1944,
                            4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9471. As conveyed by telephone (Matthews to Mosely), the War Department desires
                    to add after the words “may be agreed” the following “hereafter by U.K. and U.S.
                    military authorities (Combined Chiefs of Staff)” in the protocol on zones of
                    occupation. (Deptel 9466).</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
